Add Windows (MSVC) support to the native companion build.

Apply from the companion repository root:

    git apply companions-windows.patch

The Eden Duo checkout passed as EDEN_SOURCE_ROOT must provide the portable
DSMOD_SDK_EXPORT macro from src/core/mods/modules/dsmod_module_sdk.h
(__declspec/dllexport is not needed: the exports are named on the link line).

What it changes:

  native/modules/CMakeLists.txt
    * project(... LANGUAGES C CXX): the ooz/zstd/lz4 sources are C.
    * dsmod_add_module(): /utf-8 /bigobj and _USE_MATH_DEFINES/NOMINMAX on MSVC.
    * dsmod_add_module(): /EXPORT:<symbol> for every EXPORTS entry (no version script).
    * End of file: drops GCC/Clang-only compile options (-ffp-contract, -fno-*,
      -ffile-prefix-map, -Wall/-Wextra/-Werror/-w, -O2) from the module targets
      and from sources with per-file options.
    * dsmod-belmont: the Castlevania module (built by belmont_build.sh upstream)
      as a normal target, with lz4 from Eden's CPM cache.

  native/modules/third_party/ooz/stdafx.h
    * <intrin.h> on MSVC, builtin emulation and __forceinline macro skipped.

  native/modules/01007EF00011E000.cpp
    * BOTW_DSMOD_EXPORT instead of a bare __attribute__((visibility)) on the getters.

  native/modules/acnh_publish_diag.cpp
    * printf format attribute only on GCC/Clang.

  native/modules/p5r_recipes.h
    * _create_locale/_strtod_l (UCRT) instead of newlocale/strtod_l.

  native/modules/p5r_inventory_reader.h
    * pointer-based std::find, so the result compares with text.data() + 16.

  tools/build_dualscreen_package.py
    * windows-x86_64 is a supported module platform; its payload is <TITLEID>.dll
      and the ELF section-name hygiene check is skipped for PE images.

